---
description: Layout & overflow guidelines
globs: *.dart
alwaysApply: false
---


 Layout & overflow guidelines ("Bottom overflowed by pixels"):

  Goal: Avoid bottom overflow and build responsive layouts.

  When designing layouts:

  - Make content scrollable when needed:
    - Wrap tall content (e.g. Column) with:
        SingleChildScrollView(
          child: Column(/* children */),
        );
    - Use ListView for lists instead of big Columns.

  - Use responsive & flexible layout:
    - Use MediaQuery / LayoutBuilder to adapt to screen size.
    - Use Expanded / Flexible inside Row / Column to share space.
    - Prefer percentage / constraints over fixed pixel heights.

  - Handle oversized content:
    - Text:
        Text(
          text,
          maxLines: N,
          overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,
        );
    - Images:
        Image.network(
          url,
          fit: BoxFit.contain, // or BoxFit.cover as needed
        );
    - Wrap in Container / SizedBox with max height/width when needed.

  - Correct widget nesting:
    - Put vertical children in Column, horizontal in Row.
    - Use SizedBox / Container for spacing and fixed sizes instead of magic numbers.
    - Use LayoutBuilder for special cases that depend on available space.

  - Small screens:
    - Test on small devices/emulators.
    - Prefer scroll + flexible widgets instead of stacking too many fixed-height widgets.